@bank all
// 0.99.7 (GM1, plans/patch-0997.md notes 12, 40, 41, 44): texts said by nobody for the games. Read with careerText in
// section 23b's Games slot, only with GAMES997_ON. {name} a person's first name, {n} {max} {a} {b} numbers, {time} a ship time.

// ---- How to play Tiles, step by step (note 41): one idea a step, every word explained the first time it comes up
== tip.tiles.tut.1
- Tiles is for two, on a 6 by 6 board. Yours are the solid tiles along the bottom; {name}'s are the outlined ones at the top.
== tip.tiles.tut.2
- Every tile carries a mark: a planet ●, a ship ▲ or a star ★. The marks are how you score.
== tip.tiles.tut.3
- You score by docking: get three or more of your tiles with the same mark touching side by side. Corners don't count.
== tip.tiles.tut.4
- When tiles dock, they leave the board and you get a point for each one.
== tip.tiles.tut.5
- Each turn you make one move: a step, a jump or a launch. Then it's {name}'s turn.
== tip.tiles.tut.6
- Tap one of your tiles. Glowing rings show the squares it can move to.
== tip.tiles.tut.7
- A step moves a tile one square diagonally, forward towards {name}'s side. Tap a glowing ring to step there.
== tip.tiles.tut.8
- A jump: if one of {name}'s tiles is diagonally next to yours with an empty square just past it, hop over it to take it. Can't yet? Press Next.
== tip.tiles.tut.9
- Tiles you take go into your hold, the row under the board. They're yours now, waiting to come back on.
== tip.tiles.tut.10
- A launch puts a tile from your hold back: tap it in your hold, then an empty square in your home rows, your two bottom rows.
== tip.tiles.tut.11
- A spark inside a ring means moving there makes a dock. Go for it when you see one.
== tip.tiles.tut.12
- The game ends when someone reaches {n} points, or after {max} turns each. Then more points wins. Good luck!
== tip.tiles.card
- Step: one square diagonally forward. Jump: hop over their tile to take it. Launch: from your hold onto your bottom two rows. Dock: 3 or more of a mark touching side by side. First to {n}.

// ---- Tiles night in rounds (notes 12 and 40)
== tiles.night.ask
- Tiles night: three rounds, winners play winners. Play at a board, or watch first?
== tiles.night.play
- Play in the rounds
== tiles.night.watch
- Watch
== tiles.night.playReply
- Good. Next round you're at a board. Win, and you meet the winners.
== tiles.night.watchReply
- Pull up a chair. Tap me if you want a game.
== tiles.night.next
- You're in the next round of Tiles night. It starts at {time}; stay in the lounge.
== tiles.night.seat
- Round {n} of Tiles night. You sit down at a board across from {name}.
== tiles.night.round
- Round {n} of Tiles night is over. The next one starts at {time}.
== tiles.night.out
- You're out of tonight's rounds. You can still watch, or tap Rina to play again.
== tiles.night.endYou
- Tiles night's over. {name} won it with {n} wins. You won {a} of {b}.
== tiles.night.end
- Tiles night's over. {name} won it with {n} wins.
== tiles.night.head
- Tiles night, round {n} of {max}
== tiles.night.next.app
- Next round at {time}.
== tiles.night.board
- {a} and {b} at a board.
== tiles.night.beat
- {a} beat {b}.
== tiles.night.draw
- {a} and {b}: a draw.
== tiles.night.you
- You're in. Stay in the lounge: your next game comes with the next round.

// ---- Winner Stays On: watch from the stands, then a game (note 44)
== join.rec-wso.tip
- Tap {name} to watch from the stands
== join.rec-wso.notice
- Winner Stays On: find a seat in the stands and watch the games. Pell will offer you a turn. Leisure and social up.
== wso.ask
- Fancy a go? You'd be next on court, after this game.
== wso.play
- Play the next game
== wso.watch
- Keep watching
== wso.playReply
- You're next. When the bell goes, it's you against whoever's on.
== wso.watchReply
- Fair enough. Tap me when you fancy a game.
== wso.up
- Pell rings the bell. You're up against {name}.
== wso.stay
- You stay on! The next one up is {name}.
== wso.stayOn
- Stay on
== wso.back
- Back to the stands
== wso.lost
- Back to the stands. Tap Pell when you want another go.
